--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE SHAPE (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SharedDrivePage.tsx is the chrome-less, unauthenticated public Shared Drive report mounted at
/s/:token (web App.tsx L335, mounted before the auth shell). Single data source:
`useSharedDrive(token) → GET /share/{token}` (web useSharing.ts, retry:false, staleTime SLOW). The
page memoizes `normalizeSharedDriveData(rawData)` which collapses the v1|v2 wire union to one SI
payload (v1 lifts km→m, min→s, km/h→m·s⁻¹, Wh·km⁻¹→Wh·m⁻¹; elevation gain/loss already meters).
Render tree:
  - Loading: full-screen <Spinner/>.
  - error || !data: <ExpiredShareView/> (pin glyph + share.expired.title/description + "/" home link
    share.expired.home).
  - Success body:
    * <header>: <Logo/> + muted share.header ("Shared Drive Report").
    * Hero map (when mapPoints.length > 1): MapContainer(center, zoom 7) + MapTileLayer(dark) +
      Polyline(route) + CircleMarker(start, green) + CircleMarker(end, red).
    * Title block: h1 title + optional description + date + "start → end" endpoints.
    * Stat grid (cols default 2 / md 4): StatCard Distance(share.distance) + Duration(share.duration,
      formatDurationSecondsAsMinutes) always; then conditional Efficiency(share.efficiency,
      round(toEfficiencyDisplay(wh_per_m*1000)) + Wh/km|Wh/mi), Battery(share.battery, `${s}% → ${e}%`),
      MaxSpeed(share.maxSpeed, formatSpeed), AvgSpeed(share.avgSpeed, formatSpeed),
      ElevationGain(share.elevGain, round(convertElevation(gain)) + m|ft).
    * Vehicle GlassPanel (when data.vehicle): bolt chip + "Tesla {model}" + color.
    * Elevation ChartContainer(title share.elevation, aria share.elevation.aria) + AreaChart over
      distance (x=convertDistanceFromSI, y=convertElevation; tooltip share.elevTooltipLabel).
    * Speed ChartContainer(title share.speed, aria share.speed.aria) + LineChart over distance
      (y=convertSpeedFromSI; tooltip share.speedTooltipLabel).
    * No-map-data GlassPanel + EmptyState(share.noMapData) when map+elev+speed all empty.
    * Footer: share.footer + "Learn more →" (share.learnMore) link to the GitHub project.
Faithful, non-narrowing parity (covenant #2/#5) = reproduce every region above natively, binding
through an @Observable model that normalizes the wire to SI (web normalizeSharedDriveData), and
resolve loading / success / expired + the no-route empty branch. SI on the model, display units at
the render boundary (ADR-005). 20 web share.* literals verbatim.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Sharing/**`. That path does
NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app targets list `Sources` +
`TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,shared-surfaces}` — there
is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real, compiled canonical page home is
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**` — where the sibling P7 pages ship (power-user/SqlPlayground,
notifications/Webhooks, admin/ApiPlayground, driving/DriveDetail, …) and which `Sources` already lists
as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups, globbed). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Sharing/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Sharing`;
unit tests at `apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Sharing/**`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). Same reconciliation the sibling
notifications-Webhooks / power-user-SqlPlayground logs recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route /s/:token is token-bearing + pre-auth. The value-less `AppRoute` enum
cannot carry the token, so — exactly like the sibling token/id-bearing detail pages
(TripReplayRouteRegistration `TripReplayLink(driveID:)`, DriveDetailRouteRegistration
`DriveDetailLink(driveID:)`, which the shell hosts adopt via `.tripReplayDestination()` /
`.driveDetailDestination()`) — SharedDrive ships a typed `SharedDriveLink(token:)`
`NavigationDestination` (`.sharedDriveDestination()`), a `SharedDriveRouteRegistration.make(token:…)`
factory, and a SwiftUI-free `SharedDriveDeepLink` parser that resolves the web `/s/:token` path (and
`teslasync://s/<token>` / universal links) to a `SharedDriveLink`. Navigation registration is an
allowed file per the prompt. No `AppRoute`/`AppRouteParser` widening was needed (the existing
value-less `.sharing` case is a different, management surface).

